{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791194041,"nonce":"ZloZIuiRv6ygxymKjMXlI2QfCp4=","message":"Part fixed in 983c57152a8a432d8ced42426cdda7e13504a0f9: the shared module no longer grows after its first codegen.\n\nCause: MCJIT generates a module's code once (generateCodeForModule returns early for a loaded module, and findModuleForSymbol searches only modules not yet loaded). Every later shared promotion of a NEW function lowered its body plus queued callees into the shared module, ran default\u003cO2\u003e over the whole module, then failed with `get_function_address(Fun_N) -\u003e FunctionLookupError(Function not found in ExecutionEngine)`. The IR stayed; the function stayed on Cranelift. A promotion of a function ALREADY in the first batch also re-ran the middle end before fetching an address that already existed.\n\nNow, once the shared module is emitted:\n- a findex with a body there (not a seal_partial_bodies stub, and not under hot reload) installs that address directly;\n- anything else goes to promote_in_own_module, held to the same Low-ceiling decline the shared path applies; an own-module refusal returns the error instead of falling back to the shared path.\n\nashui ComponentsGallery, headless, release 8e2c60f vs 983c571 (--jit-log, ASH_MIDDLE_END_LOG):\n- before: 10 shared middle-end runs, shared module 12 -\u003e 156 bodies, 8 promotions failed \"not found in ExecutionEngine\"\n- after: 1 shared middle-end run, 12 bodies, 0 failures; all 8 previously failing findexes install LLVM code; 1 promotion served from the existing shared body\n- CanvasGallery: 5 -\u003e 1 shared runs; 2 failures -\u003e 0; 5 served from the shared module\nPeak footprint over a 1.5s headless run: unchanged within noise (850-933MB both arms); too short for IR to show. Needs re-measuring on the long window runs this issue was filed from.\n\nTest: crates/ash_cli/tests/shared_module_emitted.rs (ASH_PROMOTE_MODULE=0 --jit-tier llvm on PromotePhases): old binary 1 LLVM install + 8 lookup failures every run (2.97s, the failed functions stay interpreted); new 3 installs, 0 failures (0.2s).\nGates: hybrid and jit conformance isolated 1069/1069; unresolved_helper, osr_retier, parity_matrix, llvm_worker_pool, wide_hybrid, ash_core reload unit tests pass. Whole-suite threads aborts under hybrid/jit, but on 0.1.4 too: filed d34c7b9.\n\nStill open here: the first batch's IR in the shared module (it could be released once emitted, but func_cache and register_shared_bodies hold FunctionValues into it), and constants/metadata interned in the LLVMContext.","files":null}]}